description: 1) Check git status on the CURRENT ACTIVE branch (which could be 'develop' or 'dev-integration'). 2) Analyze any uncommitted changes and create one or more smart commits (max. 50 chars) on this branch. 3) After creating the commits, perform these changelog steps: a) Read the current version from `composer.json`. b) Get today's date. c) Take the messages from the commits you just created. d) Open the `CHANGLOG-2025.md` file, find today's date, and append the commit messages as new entries. If no entry for today exists, create a new heading with the date and version. e) Add the updated `CHANGLOG-2025.md` file to a new commit with the message 'Docs: Update changelog'. 4) Define the single integration branch name as `dev-integration`. 5) Push all new commits (including the changelog commit) from your current active branch to the `origin/dev-integration` branch. 6) Check if an open Pull Request from `dev-integration` to `develop` already exists. 7) If no PR exists, create a new one with the title "Integration of ongoing changes". 8) If a PR already exists, state that the existing PR has been updated. 9) Provide a link to the single, ongoing Pull Request.
alwaysApply: false
